            <ArticleTitle>Angioleiomyoma of the knee. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report a case of an angioleiomyoma at the anteromedial side of the knee mimicking a neurinoma of the infrapatellar branch of the saphenous nerve. Angioleiomyomas are benign soft tissue tumors with a predilection for the lower extremities in middle-aged females. Paroxysmal pain is triggered by pressure, cold and hormonal changes. Simple excision is usually curative.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
